$ ----------------------------------------------------------------------
$ Small nonstationary SWAN example on an unstructured triangular grid
$ Uses the same domain, forcing and output times as the regular example
$ ----------------------------------------------------------------------

PROJECT 'NSTUNSTR' '001'
SET NAUTICAL
MODE NONSTATIONARY TWODIMENSIONAL
COORDINATES CARTESIAN

$ Included Triangle mesh: 15 vertices and 16 counterclockwise triangles.
CGRID UNSTRUCTURED CIRCLE 24 0.05 1.0 32
READGRID UNSTRUCTURED TRIANGLE 'nonstationary_unstructured'

$ Regular input grids may be combined with an unstructured computation.
INPGRID BOTTOM REGULAR 0.0 0.0 0.0 1 1 2000.0 1000.0
READINP BOTTOM 1.0 'bottom.bot' 3 0 FREE

INPGRID WIND REGULAR 0.0 0.0 0.0 1 1 2000.0 1000.0 &
        NONSTATIONARY 20260101.000000 30 MIN 20260101.010000
READINP WIND 1.0 'wind.wnd' 3 0 1 0 FREE

BOUND SHAPESPEC JONSWAP 3.3 PEAK DSPR DEGREES
$ Boundary marker 1 identifies the complete western side in the .node file.
BOUNDSPEC SIDE 1 CONSTANT PAR 1.0 6.0 270.0 20.0
INITIAL PAR 0.5 5.0 270.0 25.0

GEN3 KOMEN
BREAKING CONSTANT 1.0 0.73
FRICTION JONSWAP CONSTANT 0.038

$ Interpolate each unstructured result to the regular comparison frame.
FRAME 'MAP' 0.0 0.0 0.0 2000.0 1000.0 20 10
BLOCK 'MAP' NOHEADER 'nonstationary_unstructured_hs.blk' LAYOUT 3 HSIGN &
      OUTPUT 20260101.000000 10 MIN
POINTS 'CENTER' 1000.0 500.0
TABLE 'CENTER' HEADER 'nonstationary_unstructured_center.tbl' &
      TIME TSEC XP YP WIND HSIGN TM01 DIR &
      OUTPUT 20260101.000000 10 MIN

COMPUTE NONSTATIONARY 20260101.000000 10 MIN 20260101.010000
STOP
